sentences.text:
7. The points that arise for my consideration are;
1. Whether the prosecution proves beyond all have subjected CW.1 to cruelty by harassing her both by physically and mentally and thereby committed an offence punishable U/s.498A R/w 34 of IPC ?
2. Whether the prosecution proves beyond all reasonable doubt that, on 23.11.2021 at about 7.30 AM, accused No.2 picked up quarrel with C.C.No.50373/2022 CW.1, at that time, the complainant submitted that, the accused No.1 used to consume alcohol for that she is not preparing food with a common intention assaulted CW.1 on cheeks and caused simple injuries and thereby committed an offence punishable U/s.323 R/w 34 of IPC?

opennyai_summary.decision:
12. Point No.5 :- In view of the findings on above points, I proceed to pass the following;
ORDER Acting under section 248(1) of Cr.P.C. the accused No.1 and 2 are acquitted of the offence punishable under sections 498A, 323, 504, 506 R/w 34 of Indian Penal Code.
The Bail bonds and surety bonds of the accused persons shall be in force for the period of 6 months and thereafter it shall be cancelled without further orders.

